## 🗒️ Overview

A simple Turtle graphics visualiser and recorder.  
Draw shapes interactively and automatically generate the corresponding Python Turtle code.  
Perfect for experimenting with drawing logic and exporting reusable code.

- [![bludere/TurtleVisualiser](https://img.shields.io/badge/Source-bludere%2FTurtleVisualiser-blue?logo=github)](https://github.com/bludere/TurtleVisualiser)

---

## ⚙️ Features

- **Tkinter + Turtle Canvas** — interactive drawing with keyboard bindings and mouse clicks.
- **Shape Recorder** — generates a Python script of your drawing commands in real-time.
- **Reusable Drawer Class** — `TurtleDrawer` wraps all actions for easy reuse in other projects.

---

## 📊 How It Works

- Use keyboard keys to move, rotate, draw shapes, toggle pen up/down.
- Click to set turtle position.
- Automatically writes your actions to an output `.py` file.
- Re-run the generated code anytime with standard Turtle.

---

## 🚀 Quick Start

```bash
# Clone this repository
git clone https://github.com/bludere/TurtleVisualiser.git
cd TurtleVisualiser

# Install requirements (built-in for most systems)
pip install tk

# Run the visualiser
python examples/example.py
```

